go-gostls is a pure-Go TLS 1.2 client. It is BSD-2-Clause and links no GPL
code. Its GOST cryptographic primitives come from
github.com/tarantool/go-gostcrypto (also BSD-2-Clause); it additionally depends
on filippo.io/bigmod and golang.org/x/crypto. None of these is GPL.

go-gostls is the pure-Go backend for the go-tlsdialer dialer; the alternative
cgo OpenSSL backend lives in that separate dialer module, not here.
